<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Brustem</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1467">1467</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liege-wars">Liège Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Brustem was fought on 28 October 1467 near Sint-Truiden, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, between the army of Liège and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bold">Charles the Bold</a>, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a>. The Liège militias were defeated, and the city had to accept harsh terms; after a further rising it was sacked by Charles in 1468.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-brustem.jpg" alt="Battle of Brustem" width="300" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rogier van der Weyden · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charlesletemeraire.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
